---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import TechnologyLogos from '../components/TechnologyLogos.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---
<Layout title="Home">

<section class="opening">
<div class="intro"><p class="kicker"><span class="square"></span> A PERSONAL ENGINEERING RECORD</p><h1>Built at home.<br>Learned by<br><em>doing.</em></h1><p class="dek">I’m Zachary Drake. This is a record of the systems I run, the problems I work through, and what I learn along the way.</p><a class="primary" href={`${base}projects/family-media/`}>Start with the family media project <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a class="quiet" href={`${base}professional/`}>My work in enterprise communications →</a><div class="margin-note"><span class="note-label">DESIGN REQUIREMENTS</span><p>Use what I have.<br>Understand what I’m running.<br>Make it useful for the people using it.</p></div></div>
<div class="field-record"><div class="record-top"><span>SYSTEM OVERVIEW</span><span>DL–01 / MEDIA</span></div><figure class="hero-photo"><img src={`${base}images/jellyfin-family-home.png`} alt="The family’s Jellyfin interface, with live TV, movies and shows together." width="1384" height="743"><figcaption><span class="figure-label">FIG. 01</span> The part my family sees.</figcaption></figure><div class="record-note"><span class="annotation-arrow" aria-hidden="true">+</span><div><h2>There’s a lot behind the play button.</h2><p>Linux, storage, networking, containers—and plenty of things I had to figure out the hard way.</p></div></div><div class="record-bottom"><span>REUSED HARDWARE. OPEN-SOURCE TOOLS.</span><a href={`${base}infrastructure/`}>Inspect the system →</a></div></div>
</section>
<section class="principles" aria-label="Project principles"><span class="rail-label">WORKING PRINCIPLES</span><p><b>01</b> Keep costs close to zero.</p><p><b>02</b> Keep control of the environment.</p><p><b>03</b> Make the experience simple.</p></section>
<section class="chapter"><div class="chapter-side"><p class="kicker">THE MAIN PROJECT</p><span class="folio" aria-hidden="true">01</span><p class="side-note">A family need.<br>An unexpected education.</p></div><div class="chapter-content"><p class="topic">SELF-HOSTING / USABILITY / OWNERSHIP</p><h2>A media experience<br>for my family.</h2><p class="story">It started with being tired of streaming subscriptions and disappearing catalogs. It grew into a hands-on education in building something people could actually use.</p><div class="story-grid"><div><p>Getting a service running was one lesson. Making it easy for my mom and in-laws to use was another.</p><p>Familiar clients, simpler remote access, and a way to request movies and shows all became part of the engineering.</p><a class="underlined" href={`${base}projects/family-media/`}>Read the case study <span>↗</span></a></div><figure class="request-photo" id="request-preview"><div class="request-crop"><img src={`${base}images/seerr-requests-cropped.png`} alt="Seerr’s requests interface showing movies and request availability in the administrator view." width="1398" height="736" loading="lazy"></div><figcaption><span class="figure-label">FIG. 02</span> Requests, without another text message. Administrator view shown.</figcaption></figure></div></div></section>
<section class="contents"><div class="section-intro"><p class="kicker">REFERENCE SECTIONS</p><h2>The build.<br>The reasoning.<br>The record.</h2><p>Follow the systems underneath—or the decisions that got them there.</p></div><div class="contents-list"><a href={`${base}infrastructure/`}><span class="index">A</span><div><h3>Infrastructure</h3><p>Ubuntu, containers, storage, media formats, and access.</p></div><span class="row-arrow">↗</span></a><a href={`${base}projects/`}><span class="index">B</span><div><h3>Projects</h3><p>What works today. What I want to explore next.</p></div><span class="row-arrow">↗</span></a><a href={`${base}journal/`}><span class="index">C</span><div><h3>Journal</h3><p>The mistakes, milestones, and lessons behind the setup.</p></div><span class="row-arrow">↗</span></a></div></section>
<section class="bench-note"><div><p class="kicker">A NOTE ON THE PROCESS</p><h2>Curiosity does most<br>of the connecting.</h2></div><div><p>At work, I focus on unified communications and contact center technology. At home, I have room to explore, make mistakes, and figure out unfamiliar tools.</p><p>What I learn in one environment improves how I approach the other. DrakeLabs is where I keep that thread.</p><a class="underlined" href={`${base}professional/`}>The professional side <span>↗</span></a><TechnologyLogos compact /></div></section>
<div class="colophon"><span>ABOUT THIS WEBSITE</span><p>My story and direction. Built with ChatGPT and Codex. <a href={`${base}projects/#website-process`}>How it came together →</a></p></div>

</Layout>
